jobs.description:
Are you technically skilled and looking for a full-time job as a process operator in Heerenveen? In this role, you will join a leading producer of margarines, oils, and fats. You will monitor the production process, ensure quality and safety, and directly contribute to customer satisfaction. Do you want to work in the food industry with excellent career opportunities and a great team atmosphere? Read on to discover your new challenge!

As a process operator, you will be responsible for running and supervising a modern production line where margarine, oils, and fats are manufactured and packaged. You will monitor the entire process, adjust machines when needed, and perform quality checks on finished products. With your technical insight and attention to detail, you make sure production runs smoothly, safely, and according to the highest quality standards.

This is a 3-shift schedule position, giving you variety in your work as well as extra free time. It’s a dynamic role with plenty of opportunities to grow and develop.

We are looking for a process operator with the following skills and qualifications:

- Technical affinity or work experience as an operator/process operator;

- Experience in a production environment, preferably in the food industry;

- Motivated, eager to learn, and detail-oriented;

- Strong focus on quality, hygiene, and safety;

- Availability for a full-time 40-hour work week;

- Willingness to work in a 3-shift schedule;

- Good command of the Dutch or English language (spoken and written).

Are you an experienced Reach Truck Driver looking for a new opportunity? We are currently recruiting for a modern logistics company in Helmond. As a Reach Truck Driver, you will be responsible for safely and efficiently moving goods throughout the warehouse while supporting daily logistics operations using modern equipment.

Your responsibilities:

- Operating a reach truck at heights of up to 12 meters;
- Moving and storing pallets throughout the warehouse;
- Picking orders using the reach truck;
- Scanning, labeling, and wrapping pallets;
- Checking orders before shipment;
- Supporting Value Added Services (VAS) activities;
- Maintaining a clean, safe, and organized working environment.

Working Hours in the day shift: 07:00 AM – 04:00 PM. During peak periods in July till October, a two-shift schedule may be required. (6:00-15:00/15:00-00:00)

- Holds a valid Reach Truck certificate;
- Is comfortable working at heights up to 12 meters;
- Fulltime available;
- Living nearby Helmond, Mierlo, Geldrop, Nuenen or Eindhoven;
- Has experience in logistics and safety;
- Is flexible regarding tasks and working hours;
- Has a good command of Dutch and/or English.

Are you looking for a fulltime job in logistics? Would you like to work in a modern, international warehouse where fashion and clothing products are shipped to customers all over the world? Then this opportunity could be perfect for you!

For a large logistics clothing warehouse in Lelystad, we are looking for motivated Production Workers, Warehouse Operatives, and Logistics Associates. You will become part of a friendly international team where teamwork, quality, and a positive working atmosphere are key. On top of that, you can enjoy a delicious hot lunch every working day.

As a Production Worker in the warehouse, you will help ensure that all goods are processed efficiently and accurately. Your tasks will include:

- Loading and unloading trucks;
- Picking and packing customer orders;
- Checking products for quality;
- Unpacking boxes and processing incoming goods;
- Sorting clothing and accessories;
- Maintaining a clean and safe working environment.

This is a full-time position in a 2-shift rotation:

- Morning shift: 07:00 AM - 03:30 PM
- Afternoon shift: 03:00 PM - 11:30 PM

But there is also a nightshift you can work if you want from 23:00 tot 07:30. And there is work in the weekends!

- (Basic) English communication skills, or Polish or Spanish;
- Availability for full-time work in a 2-shift schedule;
- Ability to work effectively in a team;
- Physically fit and comfortable performing active warehouse work;
- Attention to detail and ability to follow instructions;
- Previous logistics or warehouse experience is a plus, but not required.
